  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The novel treats space path as one of the two foundational Gu Master paths that form the basis of heaven and earth, not as a generic word for teleportation.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Since the immemorial era there were two types of Gu Masters, space path and time path. Space path represented up, down, left, and right, while time path represented past, present, and future. Blessed land size is measured against that spatial frame, just as time flow is measured against the temporal one.",
      "chapters": [
        383
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-the-path-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters",
        "sys_blessed_lands_and_grotto_heavens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Tu Shi Cheng places space path and time path in Ren Zu’s time during the Immemorial Antiquity Era as the two paths that researched and expounded on the profundities of time and space. When Gu Master cultivation first flourished, space path and time path were the mainstream paths before wisdom path, qi path, strength path, rule path, and others emerged in turn.",
      "chapters": [
        1323
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "immemorial-with-time",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_tu_shi_cheng",
        "char_ren_zu",
        "evt_era_immemorial"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A space path Gu Immortal of Yi clan is named the clan’s strongest rank seven expert and a blood-related successor of the first supreme elder. Fang Yuan obtains a space path Immortal Gu that looks like a blue jade sphere with a pair of snow-white wings, while noting that he does not cultivate space path, has only ordinary attainment in it, and lacks many space path dao marks.",
      "chapters": [
        1608
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "ordinary-attainment-and-immortal-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "fac_yi_clan",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Giant Sun Immortal Venerable states that Thieving Heaven cultivates theft path primarily with space path as the secondary path, matching the venerable pattern of one main path and one specialty path.",
      "chapters": [
        2203
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "thieving-heaven-secondary",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_giant_sun_immortal_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A later stretch repeats the same pairing: Thieving Heaven Demon Venerable cultivated theft path and space path.",
      "chapters": [
        2204
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
